### The test issuer's key set, published in the sink before anyone signs in. The discovery document is a committed
### mapping; the key it points at is this machine's (_shared/TestIssuer.csx), so it is registered per run — an
### import with a fixed stub id, which replaces the stub a previous run left rather than adding a second one.
# @name PublishIssuerKeys
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsSinkUrl}}/__admin/mappings/import
Content-Type: application/json

{{IssuerKeySetImport}}

### What Alvo reads at the issuer's jwks_uri (the sink shares Alvo's loopback, so :9090 there is :8083 here)
# @name IssuerKeys
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsSinkUrl}}/oidc/jwks.json

### RFC 8414 metadata: where a client exchanges an ID token, and the keys Alvo's own tokens verify against
# @name Metadata
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server

### Dana signs in: an RFC 8693 token exchange of her Google ID token for an Alvo session
# @name DanaSignIn
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Atoken-exchange&subject_token={{DanaIdToken}}&subject_token_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Atoken-type%3Aid_token

### A forgery: Olga's claims and the published `kid`, signed by a key the issuer never published
# @name ForgedSignIn
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Atoken-exchange&subject_token={{OlgaForgedIdToken}}&subject_token_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Atoken-type%3Aid_token

### A properly signed token minted for another client's `aud`
# @name WrongAudienceSignIn
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Atoken-exchange&subject_token={{OlgaWrongAudienceIdToken}}&subject_token_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Atoken-type%3Aid_token

### A properly signed token for our `aud` whose `azp` names another client (#544)
# @name ForeignAzpSignIn
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Atoken-exchange&subject_token={{OlgaForeignAzpIdToken}}&subject_token_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Atoken-type%3Aid_token

### Theo signs in
# @name TheoSignIn
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Atoken-exchange&subject_token={{TheoIdToken}}&subject_token_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Atoken-type%3Aid_token

### Olga signs in with her real ID token
# @name OlgaSignIn
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Atoken-exchange&subject_token={{OlgaIdToken}}&subject_token_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Atoken-type%3Aid_token

### Dana's ID token again: it was valid a moment ago, and it has already started a session
# @name DanaReplaysIdToken
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [400]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Atoken-exchange&subject_token={{DanaIdToken}}&subject_token_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Atoken-type%3Aid_token

### Who Dana is to Alvo
# @name DanaUser
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/user
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaSignIn.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Who Theo is
# @name TheoUser
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/user
Authorization: Bearer {{TheoSignIn.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Who Olga is
# @name OlgaUser
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/user
Authorization: Bearer {{OlgaSignIn.response.body.$.access_token}}

### The run's own region, by the only caller `regions.create` admits — the later cases' jobs point at it
# @name AdminCreatesRegion
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "{{RegionCode}}",
  "name": "Self-service region {{RegionCode}}"
}
